Package: ferrus
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.6), libadwaita-1-0 (>= 1.2), policykit-1, util-linux (>= 2.38), dosfstools, ntfs-3g | ntfsprogs, wimtools, e2fsprogs
Recommends: exfatprogs, udftools
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Ferrus Developers <ferrus@localhost>
Homepage: https://example.invalid/ferrus
Description: Bootable USB creation tool for Linux
 A native Rufus-style utility that writes ISO images and Windows
 installers to USB drives: raw DD for Linux ISOs, FAT32 layouts with
 automatic WIM splitting for Windows, UEFI:NTFS for oversized trees,
 GPT/MBR partition schemes, filesystem/cluster/label control and
 optional bad-block scanning.
